------------What is there in meta-layers ?------------
- A meta-layer is essentially a collection of metadata. The recipes available in the meta-layer are .bb files
( plus any modifications via .bbappend files )
e.g. 
        meta/
        ├── recipes-core/
        ├── recipes-devtools/
        ├── recipes-kernel/
        ├── recipes-connectivity/
        ├── recipes-extended/
        ├── recipes-support/
        ├── recipes-graphics/
        └── ...
The hierarchy inside these recipes looks somewhat like - 
            meta/
            └── recipes-core/
                ├── busybox/
                │   └── busybox_1.36.1.bb
                ├── systemd/
                │   └── systemd_257.bb
                └── glibc/
                    └── glibc_2.41.bb

                
      


